WEBVTT

00:00:01.520 --> 00:00:04.020
Space has laws, but no rules.

00:00:04.020 --> 00:00:07.070
Out there, playing by the book can get you killed.

00:00:07.070 --> 00:00:10.550
Although manuals exist for things like

00:00:10.550 --> 00:00:12.780
piracy, electronic warfare, and FTL jumps,

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:15.240
in a pinch, the crew's decisions,

00:00:15.240 --> 00:00:19.370
especially those of the captain,
will determine the ship's fate.

00:00:19.370 --> 00:00:22.040
With the yacht club aboard the Bentenmaru,

00:00:22.040 --> 00:00:24.710
are Kato Marika's skills up to the task?

00:00:25.030 --> 00:00:26.040
It's impossible...

00:00:26.040 --> 00:00:30.000
We launched at low propulsion,
so the propellant hasn't stabilized.

00:00:30.540 --> 00:00:31.880
Marika...

00:00:31.880 --> 00:00:33.010
We'll jump.

00:02:04.040 --> 00:02:06.520
Let's eat!

00:02:08.740 --> 00:02:10.130
This is great.

00:02:16.670 --> 00:02:21.320
I was worried for a little while,
but I'm glad everything worked out.

00:02:21.600 --> 00:02:23.800
It's too early to lower your guard.

00:02:23.800 --> 00:02:25.690
We're just getting started.

00:02:25.690 --> 00:02:27.470
That's true, but...

00:02:27.470 --> 00:02:30.460
Well, we should at least relax during dinner.

00:02:30.910 --> 00:02:33.070
Curry is delicious, isn't it?

00:02:33.070 --> 00:02:34.630
I've never had it before.

00:02:34.630 --> 00:02:37.700
Haramaki really is a good cook.

00:02:37.700 --> 00:02:39.480
I love it too.

00:02:39.480 --> 00:02:41.470
Who wants seconds?

00:02:41.800 --> 00:02:43.290
I'll have some.

00:02:43.290 --> 00:02:44.720
Haramaki, me too.

00:02:45.020 --> 00:02:46.250
On it.

00:02:46.250 --> 00:02:49.090
We can do FTL jumps now.

00:02:49.090 --> 00:02:52.880
Tomorrow, we should start practicing our piracy.

00:02:52.880 --> 00:02:55.730
We're done for today though, right?

00:02:55.730 --> 00:02:56.690
No, we aren't.

00:02:57.620 --> 00:02:59.430
D-Did I forget something?

00:02:59.430 --> 00:03:00.600
Room assignments.

00:03:00.600 --> 00:03:01.870
Where is everyone going to sleep?

00:03:01.870 --> 00:03:03.950
Oh yeah...

00:03:04.240 --> 00:03:05.490
I forgot.

00:03:07.850 --> 00:03:08.910
Thanks for the food!

00:03:11.490 --> 00:03:14.390
As harsh as ever, Chiaki.

00:03:14.390 --> 00:03:15.250
You think so?

00:03:15.700 --> 00:03:17.840
As a fellow pirate,

00:03:17.840 --> 00:03:21.510
you want Marika to improve as fast as she can, right?

00:03:21.790 --> 00:03:23.500
That's not it.

00:03:23.500 --> 00:03:26.300
Wouldn't you guys be upset if you had nowhere to sleep?

00:03:29.880 --> 00:03:32.940
The taste of passion: capsaicin.

00:03:37.030 --> 00:03:39.820
I bet the Bentenmaru's serving dinner now.

00:03:40.110 --> 00:03:42.460
Can Marika cook?

00:03:42.460 --> 00:03:44.450
One of the yacht club members can.

00:03:44.450 --> 00:03:45.780
So it'll be fine.

00:03:46.160 --> 00:03:48.610
Still, is this really okay?

00:03:48.610 --> 00:03:53.610
They can FTL jump, but they can't tune the converter reactors.

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:56.520
And it isn't a good idea to work the alpha reactor too hard.

00:03:59.150 --> 00:04:00.420
I can't see anything.

00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.080
I hope they can keep it running.

00:04:03.080 --> 00:04:06.890
If you're worried, I can turn on another on-board camera.

00:04:07.630 --> 00:04:10.890
There are others besides the one
that the Kurihara girl destroyed.

00:04:10.890 --> 00:04:13.910
Let's let them try to handle things themselves for now.

00:04:20.640 --> 00:04:22.150
Is everything okay?

00:04:22.510 --> 00:04:23.870
Just fine.

00:04:23.870 --> 00:04:24.900
Goodnight.

00:04:25.390 --> 00:04:26.660
Goodnight.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:33.010
Looks fine in here.

00:04:34.150 --> 00:04:35.170
Goodnight.

00:04:37.730 --> 00:04:38.920
Is everything oka—

00:04:40.390 --> 00:04:41.850
Sorry...

00:04:41.850 --> 00:04:43.500
We're fine.

00:04:43.500 --> 00:04:46.840
Goodnight!

00:04:51.050 --> 00:04:53.610
President, it's almost lights out.

00:04:53.610 --> 00:04:54.690
Oh, roger.

00:04:55.280 --> 00:04:58.150
Will you be all right up here alone?

00:04:58.150 --> 00:05:01.070
Yeah, I'll have someone take over later.

00:05:01.070 --> 00:05:03.110
Besides, there's a lot I want to review.

00:05:03.410 --> 00:05:05.450
Okay then.

00:05:05.450 --> 00:05:06.760
Night.

00:05:06.760 --> 00:05:07.920
Goodnight.

00:05:12.010 --> 00:05:13.790
So tired...

00:05:14.070 --> 00:05:17.000
You should get to sleep or you'll
have a hard time tomorrow.

00:05:28.000 --> 00:05:29.500
That fast?

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:30.560
Why?

00:05:32.300 --> 00:05:33.520
Yeah...

00:05:35.990 --> 00:05:37.020
I see.

00:05:37.780 --> 00:05:39.330
Got it.

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:40.980
I'll talk to you later.

00:05:41.420 --> 00:05:43.930
Yeah, I'll handle it.

00:05:43.930 --> 00:05:44.940
Bye.

00:05:49.370 --> 00:05:50.320
President?

00:05:51.430 --> 00:05:53.290
It's time to change shifts.

00:05:54.740 --> 00:05:55.920
Got it.

00:05:55.920 --> 00:05:56.910
Thanks.

00:06:16.130 --> 00:06:17.440
I overslept!

00:06:21.470 --> 00:06:23.650
Marika, good morning.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:25.180
Morning.

00:06:25.180 --> 00:06:26.190
S-Sorry.

00:06:26.670 --> 00:06:28.600
You should have woken me up.

00:06:28.600 --> 00:06:30.170
You were out cold.

00:06:30.170 --> 00:06:32.910
And Gruier did try to wake you.

00:06:34.640 --> 00:06:36.010
I did.

00:06:36.010 --> 00:06:39.080
Slaps, pinches... I tried everything.

00:06:40.590 --> 00:06:41.880
I'm in despair...

00:06:41.880 --> 00:06:45.100
You must have been really tired after yesterday.

00:06:45.100 --> 00:06:46.840
Y-Yeah...

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:49.800
Go on, get changed.

00:07:00.510 --> 00:07:03.900
Captain Marika of the Bentenmaru has arrived.

00:07:04.580 --> 00:07:05.970
We've been waiting for this!

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:07.280
You look so cool.

00:07:07.640 --> 00:07:10.530
You look wonderful in that outfit.

00:07:10.530 --> 00:07:13.160
Marika really is a pirate.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:15.450
It suits her.

00:07:15.450 --> 00:07:16.690
It's really great.

00:07:18.530 --> 00:07:21.320
Um, that's enough clapping.

00:07:22.630 --> 00:07:26.130
Okay. I'll go over our pirate job.

00:07:27.810 --> 00:07:30.620
This is the luxury liner, Princess Apricot.

00:07:30.620 --> 00:07:32.840
It's our target this time.

00:07:33.560 --> 00:07:37.350
But they are also regular customers.

00:07:37.350 --> 00:07:40.100
They have provided us with information, and they trust us.

00:07:42.140 --> 00:07:45.860
You can think of piracy as a stage show for a luxury liner.

00:07:46.410 --> 00:07:49.570
The whole thing is planned,
so it isn't too dangerous.

00:07:50.020 --> 00:07:52.010
And you don't need to worry about any unplanned accidents.

00:07:52.710 --> 00:07:53.760
Oh.

00:07:53.760 --> 00:07:56.220
This might be easier than I expected.

00:07:56.220 --> 00:07:58.180
It isn't that simple.

00:08:01.450 --> 00:08:03.070
Chiaki's right.

00:08:03.070 --> 00:08:07.000
There's more to piracy than simply flying the ship.

00:08:07.000 --> 00:08:08.250
There are procedures.

00:08:08.630 --> 00:08:09.730
Procedures?

00:08:09.730 --> 00:08:10.460
Yes.

00:08:10.940 --> 00:08:15.180
First, we FTL jump in front of the Princess Apricot,

00:08:15.180 --> 00:08:16.700
and we ambush them.

00:08:16.700 --> 00:08:19.930
Captain, about that...

00:08:19.930 --> 00:08:24.090
I realized this during our last jump...

00:08:24.090 --> 00:08:27.900
Relying on the alpha reactor alone is a little dangerous.

00:08:28.160 --> 00:08:30.950
She's right. Otherwise, why have two?

00:08:31.940 --> 00:08:38.370
So I thought about it, and I wondered if we could use the alpha and beta together.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:44.330
Raise the alpha output a little, then make minor stabilization adjustments to beta,

00:08:44.330 --> 00:08:46.210
and it should work.

00:08:47.020 --> 00:08:49.960
Or maybe we shouldn't?

00:08:50.270 --> 00:08:53.340
No, that's really smart!

00:08:53.340 --> 00:08:56.720
My family's cruiser is a two-engine too.

00:08:56.720 --> 00:08:58.930
And sometimes, when one is out-of-whack,

00:08:59.360 --> 00:09:01.140
that's how we do it.

00:09:02.080 --> 00:09:03.610
I'll leave it to you.

00:09:03.610 --> 00:09:06.420
Yayoi can oversee the engine.

00:09:07.540 --> 00:09:08.860
Thank you.

00:09:09.460 --> 00:09:13.920
Once we have a visual on the cruise ship, we'll initiate electronic warfare.

00:09:13.920 --> 00:09:18.070
We'll take over their controls and announce ourselves.

00:09:20.990 --> 00:09:21.950
President?

00:09:21.950 --> 00:09:24.060
Y-Yeah?

00:09:24.060 --> 00:09:26.140
That's my job, right?

00:09:26.140 --> 00:09:28.070
Don't overdo it.

00:09:28.070 --> 00:09:29.960
Yeah... I know.

00:09:31.920 --> 00:09:33.920
Then it gets hard again.

00:09:34.210 --> 00:09:38.590
After touchdown, we have to get in close to the liner.

00:09:38.590 --> 00:09:40.410
We need to keep the customers entertained,

00:09:40.410 --> 00:09:44.140
so we'll have to dock by force at a range visible from the windows.

00:09:44.420 --> 00:09:46.570
Keep them entertained?

00:09:46.570 --> 00:09:48.470
For how long?

00:09:48.470 --> 00:09:49.730
Two or three minutes, I guess?

00:09:51.380 --> 00:09:54.290
Even entering port takes longer than that...

00:09:54.290 --> 00:09:56.820
We can't keep the customers waiting.

00:09:56.820 --> 00:10:02.050
Not only can we not keep them waiting, if we mess up the docking and damage their ship,

00:10:02.050 --> 00:10:03.670
we'll have to pay a penalty.

00:10:03.670 --> 00:10:04.790
R-Really?

00:10:04.790 --> 00:10:06.490
Come on, Chiaki.

00:10:06.490 --> 00:10:08.100
Don't scare them.

00:10:08.100 --> 00:10:13.280
And once you've boarded their ship,
you do your piracy duties,

00:10:13.280 --> 00:10:15.510
then return to the Bentenmaru, and you're done.

00:10:24.140 --> 00:10:27.850
Will I be able to do something that hard?

00:10:27.850 --> 00:10:32.400
Didn't you win the middle school tournament?

00:10:32.400 --> 00:10:34.230
Yeah, but that was in a yacht.

00:10:34.230 --> 00:10:39.610
But I don't know if I can pilot a spaceship through complex maneuvers when I've never been on one before.

00:10:39.610 --> 00:10:42.990
We are beginners, after all.

00:10:43.920 --> 00:10:46.690
You can't start complaining now.

00:10:46.690 --> 00:10:47.890
You must do it.

00:10:49.340 --> 00:10:51.310
I'm sorry for being so harsh.

00:10:51.310 --> 00:10:54.040
But we can't back out now.

00:10:54.890 --> 00:10:59.550
I know it's my fault that you're all involved,

00:10:59.890 --> 00:11:01.830
but I will not let you fail.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:04.510
So I want you to believe in and follow me.

00:11:09.900 --> 00:11:11.350
I'll go with you.

00:11:11.960 --> 00:11:12.560
What about you guys?

00:11:13.410 --> 00:11:14.320
Of course.

00:11:14.600 --> 00:11:17.030
I'm sorry for saying something so strange.

00:11:17.030 --> 00:11:18.440
Sorry, Marika.

00:11:18.940 --> 00:11:21.780
I'll help with the helm as much as I can.

00:11:21.780 --> 00:11:23.070
Thank you!

00:11:23.690 --> 00:11:26.040
I shall also help, Captain.

00:11:27.850 --> 00:11:31.170
I know I'm late in saying this, but thanks, everyone.

00:11:38.310 --> 00:11:38.960
Now...

00:11:38.960 --> 00:11:41.010
It's time for some piracy!

00:11:52.780 --> 00:11:54.770
A message from navigation:

00:11:55.240 --> 00:12:01.410
The Princess Apricot is presently
at Galactic Corridor West-40.68, B-Post.

00:12:01.410 --> 00:12:05.020
We are currently approaching the Rainbow Cluster.

00:12:10.470 --> 00:12:14.040
It is 21:00 hours, Galactic Standard Time.

00:12:14.040 --> 00:12:17.960
It is now night in the main hall.

00:12:17.960 --> 00:12:24.680
Please enjoy your journey through the stars
upon the Princess Apricot.

00:12:25.110 --> 00:12:26.840
No! Not that button!

00:12:26.840 --> 00:12:29.060
What? We're already in?

00:12:32.740 --> 00:12:34.550
Ah, excuse me.

00:12:34.550 --> 00:12:38.500
This is Captain Marika of the Bentenmaru!

00:12:40.370 --> 00:12:41.780
We've been waiting for this!

00:12:41.780 --> 00:12:46.380
The Bentenmaru has completed its electronic
attack on the Princess Apricot's systems.

00:12:46.380 --> 00:12:47.690
No!

00:12:47.690 --> 00:12:49.690
What? It's not complete?

00:12:51.250 --> 00:12:54.710
U-Um... We're about to complete our attack.

00:12:55.660 --> 00:12:57.540
They're not up to their usual standard.

00:12:59.120 --> 00:13:03.490
The transponder and Captain Marika's voiceprint match.

00:13:03.490 --> 00:13:06.180
Then, they're not impostors at least.

00:13:06.500 --> 00:13:09.000
I apologize for the mistakes.

00:13:09.000 --> 00:13:13.140
We ask the captain to please prepare
all items for surrender to the Bentenmaru.

00:13:13.500 --> 00:13:17.730
We're in the process of docking with the Princess Apricot.

00:13:17.730 --> 00:13:19.940
Resistance is futile!

00:13:21.940 --> 00:13:24.720
That was pretty rough.

00:13:24.720 --> 00:13:29.780
Detailed tactical planning and careful piloting
are the Bentenmaru's selling points too.

00:13:30.340 --> 00:13:35.070
Maybe their normal crew is ill,
and they have trainees today?

00:13:35.070 --> 00:13:36.540
Nah.

00:13:40.170 --> 00:13:41.840
Attention all passengers:

00:13:41.840 --> 00:13:45.170
This is Ronald Harley, Captain of the Princess Apricot.

00:13:47.420 --> 00:13:51.900
The pirates of the Bentenmaru are preparing to board,

00:13:51.900 --> 00:13:53.600
but there's no need to fear.

00:13:53.600 --> 00:13:57.100
Let us welcome them with applause.

00:13:57.640 --> 00:14:01.120
I've never seen a pirate before.

00:14:01.120 --> 00:14:02.550
Neither have I!

00:14:02.550 --> 00:14:04.690
This will be a valuable experience.

00:14:04.690 --> 00:14:06.820
It'll be a great story to tell.

00:14:22.060 --> 00:14:26.510
I'm Captain Marika, of the pirate ship Bentenmaru.

00:14:26.510 --> 00:14:29.520
I am here to plunder the Princess Apricot.

00:14:29.520 --> 00:14:31.300
I apologize for the rudeness.

00:14:42.400 --> 00:14:43.590
Cosplay?

00:14:43.590 --> 00:14:47.280
I thought the Bentenmaru was
a more straight-laced group.

00:14:47.280 --> 00:14:48.530
Maybe they're rebranding?

00:14:48.530 --> 00:14:49.990
What is this?

00:14:52.980 --> 00:14:53.900
Jeez...

00:14:53.900 --> 00:14:56.210
The customers are getting suspicious!

00:14:56.210 --> 00:14:58.780
Should we go and assist?

00:14:58.780 --> 00:15:01.540
Gruier, given our position,

00:15:01.540 --> 00:15:03.920
that could be a problem for Miss Marika.

00:15:04.500 --> 00:15:07.380
What should we do about this?

00:15:09.290 --> 00:15:11.970
Um, that was a warning shot.

00:15:12.470 --> 00:15:15.690
I repeat. We are pirates.

00:15:15.690 --> 00:15:18.200
Please don't forget that.

00:15:19.680 --> 00:15:24.150
As long as you follow our orders,
we will guarantee your safety.

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:27.110
Follow our orders, okay?

00:15:27.800 --> 00:15:30.500
Come on, get moving!

00:15:31.130 --> 00:15:33.620
Please stay calm!

00:15:34.020 --> 00:15:40.610
We are pirates after all.

00:15:40.610 --> 00:15:45.340
Hand over all of your treasure.

00:15:49.400 --> 00:15:50.930
They're enjoying themselves.

00:15:50.930 --> 00:15:51.590
So it would seem...

00:15:51.590 --> 00:15:54.800
I wanted to go too.

00:15:55.910 --> 00:15:58.890
Where did those outfits come from anyway?

00:15:58.890 --> 00:16:01.310
Mami gave them to us.

00:16:01.310 --> 00:16:01.980
Mami did?

00:16:02.550 --> 00:16:05.940
When we picked up those snacks at the Lamp House,

00:16:05.940 --> 00:16:09.740
she said we shouldn't wear our uniforms while pirating.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:13.560
She didn't sleep for three days
so she could make those.

00:16:13.560 --> 00:16:15.710
That sounds just like her.

00:16:15.710 --> 00:16:17.490
Choosing cosplay outfits, that is.

00:16:18.240 --> 00:16:21.710
I hope it doesn't become a habit.

00:16:24.720 --> 00:16:26.970
Thank you for your cooperation.

00:16:26.970 --> 00:16:28.380
Thank you.

00:16:30.020 --> 00:16:31.700
You're cute.

00:16:31.700 --> 00:16:32.940
How old are you?

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:34.110
Do you have a boyfriend?

00:16:35.700 --> 00:16:37.930
Would you like to have some tea later?

00:16:39.540 --> 00:16:42.620
Did you forget that we're pirates?

00:16:42.620 --> 00:16:44.270
Sorry!

00:16:49.010 --> 00:16:51.150
This is from our captain.

00:16:51.500 --> 00:16:53.630
Oh, really?

00:16:53.630 --> 00:16:56.160
Show of the insurance company asked him to prepare it.

00:16:56.660 --> 00:17:00.870
And the customers appear to be
enjoying themselves more than usual.

00:17:01.410 --> 00:17:02.910
I see.

00:17:02.910 --> 00:17:07.890
We were worried because your approach was rocky, but...

00:17:09.340 --> 00:17:15.720
Well, this is a strange thing for a victim of piracy to say,
but we look forward to further business.

00:17:16.340 --> 00:17:18.180
As do we.

00:17:28.580 --> 00:17:29.940
Now,

00:17:30.200 --> 00:17:32.690
let's celebrate our successful piracy.

00:17:33.020 --> 00:17:34.150
Cheers!

00:17:34.390 --> 00:17:36.970
Cheers!

00:17:38.410 --> 00:17:39.320
Say cheese.

00:17:44.410 --> 00:17:49.030
I was worried for a bit, but it all worked out.

00:17:49.030 --> 00:17:51.570
You were so nervous, Ai.

00:17:51.570 --> 00:17:54.490
But you piloted it just fine.

00:17:54.490 --> 00:17:56.300
Thank you.

00:17:56.300 --> 00:17:59.050
Everyone really enjoyed themselves.

00:17:59.050 --> 00:18:01.020
You more than anyone.

00:18:01.020 --> 00:18:02.230
No!

00:18:02.230 --> 00:18:05.060
Not at all!

00:18:05.390 --> 00:18:08.210
Next time, I want to try a different outfit.

00:18:08.210 --> 00:18:11.020
Yeah. I'm thinking ninja next time!

00:18:11.930 --> 00:18:16.990
Either way, everyone did really well for your first times.

00:18:17.450 --> 00:18:18.520
Thank you.

00:18:18.520 --> 00:18:20.110
You're welcome.

00:18:20.110 --> 00:18:22.120
Any time!

00:18:22.760 --> 00:18:25.520
Really, it looked like such fun.

00:18:25.520 --> 00:18:29.430
Do you think I could try it on the Barbalusa sometime?

00:18:29.430 --> 00:18:30.600
No way.

00:18:30.600 --> 00:18:32.890
Just remember your position.

00:18:38.140 --> 00:18:41.180
You eat too, Marika.

00:18:41.180 --> 00:18:43.120
It will be gone soon.

00:18:43.120 --> 00:18:44.140
Y-Yeah.

00:18:46.310 --> 00:18:47.400
So tired...

00:18:47.400 --> 00:18:48.450
Wait.

00:18:49.390 --> 00:18:52.090
You can't fall asleep like that.

00:18:52.090 --> 00:18:56.490
Change into your pajamas,
brush your teeth, then go to sleep.

00:18:56.490 --> 00:18:57.110
Got it?

00:18:58.160 --> 00:18:59.670
Right...

00:19:00.420 --> 00:19:03.460
You sound like a mother.

00:19:03.460 --> 00:19:05.240
Sorry to be annoying.

00:19:06.510 --> 00:19:08.320
No, it's the opposite.

00:19:08.320 --> 00:19:11.210
Ririka rarely says stuff like that.

00:19:12.950 --> 00:19:13.960
Thanks.

00:19:16.990 --> 00:19:21.640
Come to think of it,
wasn't Lynn acting a little strange?

00:19:22.940 --> 00:19:26.700
She seemed kind of distracted.

00:19:27.460 --> 00:19:28.640
Really?

00:19:28.640 --> 00:19:29.730
Perhaps she was just tired.

00:19:32.020 --> 00:19:33.180
I wonder what's wrong.

00:19:35.400 --> 00:19:37.610
Sorry to bother you when you're resting.

00:19:37.610 --> 00:19:39.190
I have to talk to you.

00:19:43.840 --> 00:19:46.080
It's about President Lynn...

00:19:46.560 --> 00:19:50.840
Grunhilde saw her communicating with someone.

00:19:50.840 --> 00:19:54.530
It sounded important.

00:19:54.530 --> 00:19:56.440
Speaking with someone on the outside?

00:19:56.440 --> 00:19:58.250
What were they discussing?

00:19:58.250 --> 00:19:59.750
I don't know.

00:19:59.750 --> 00:20:01.260
I couldn't hear.

00:20:01.960 --> 00:20:05.010
It kind of stuck with me, so I kept an eye on her,

00:20:05.600 --> 00:20:07.220
and I saw her doing it a few more times.

00:20:08.100 --> 00:20:10.480
Who was she talking with?

00:20:10.750 --> 00:20:14.020
I should have asked her at the time.

00:20:14.020 --> 00:20:17.440
But it didn't seem as though I could.

00:20:20.410 --> 00:20:24.660
I don't want to say this,
but perhaps she's a spy.

00:20:26.080 --> 00:20:27.770
I hate to admit it,

00:20:27.770 --> 00:20:32.330
but that's why I originally joined the yacht club.

00:20:33.410 --> 00:20:35.230
It is possible.

00:20:37.250 --> 00:20:42.300
And the president was put on
probation in middle school for cracking, correct?

00:20:43.100 --> 00:20:45.760
Maybe someone hired her for her skills,

00:20:45.760 --> 00:20:48.720
and that's what brought her to the Bentenmaru.

00:20:50.970 --> 00:20:53.610
So she's a pirate too?

00:20:53.610 --> 00:20:55.850
Or part of another organization?

00:20:59.580 --> 00:21:02.530
No, I don't think so.

00:21:04.030 --> 00:21:05.530
Let's ask her ourselves.

00:21:09.570 --> 00:21:11.700
I thought you might call for me soon.

00:21:13.160 --> 00:21:16.370
Then you know why you're here.

00:21:16.370 --> 00:21:17.650
More or less.

00:21:17.650 --> 00:21:20.420
I figured you'd pick up on it, Marika.

00:21:21.050 --> 00:21:23.450
I am the captain after all.

00:21:26.790 --> 00:21:28.550
So let's hear it.

00:21:29.320 --> 00:21:31.850
Who were you talking with?

00:21:38.870 --> 00:21:40.980
What's wrong?

00:21:44.420 --> 00:21:48.110
Actually, I have a job for the Bentenmaru.

00:21:49.290 --> 00:21:50.530
A job?

00:21:51.430 --> 00:21:57.000
I wish to kidnap the former president of the
Hakuoh Academy Yacht Club, Jenny Dolittle.

00:21:57.890 --> 00:21:58.750
Kidnap?

00:22:04.840 --> 00:22:08.260
True darkness feels so empty.

00:22:08.260 --> 00:22:11.260
The Hakuoh Pirates' First Job

00:22:11.260 --> 00:22:18.520
I can't even see my own palm.

00:22:18.520 --> 00:22:24.820
The stars above are the only light.

00:22:24.820 --> 00:22:32.120
My senses sharpen again, like a wild animal's.

00:22:32.120 --> 00:22:35.160
My conscience heads inward, inward

00:22:35.160 --> 00:22:37.500
on an arduous, testing journey.

00:22:38.670 --> 00:22:41.790
The fragile blade I believed in

00:22:42.340 --> 00:22:46.170
lost its shine.

00:22:47.630 --> 00:22:54.310
Into the holy space I throw myself.

00:22:54.600 --> 00:23:01.190
Find the answer no matter how hard, Black Holy.

00:23:01.190 --> 00:23:07.990
Although I'm bad at calculating while moving forward,

00:23:08.360 --> 00:23:18.040
I knew that it was alright to do things naturally.

00:23:19.160 --> 00:23:26.880
Hey, try to open your eyes once again,

00:23:26.880 --> 00:23:31.720
even if it's just somewhere you went to see the stars.

00:23:38.820 --> 00:23:40.440
Their job was a success.

00:23:41.010 --> 00:23:44.480
But Lynn, the new yacht club
president, has a job for them.

00:23:44.970 --> 00:23:46.250
What problem affects

00:23:46.250 --> 00:23:48.690
the former president Jenny Dolittle?

00:23:49.830 --> 00:23:52.610
Corporate fleet cannon blasts assail the Bentenmaru.

00:23:54.150 --> 00:23:55.930
Next time, on <i>Bodacious Space Pirates:</i>

00:23:55.930 --> 00:23:57.580
A surprising client.

00:23:57.580 --> 00:23:58.950
Look forward to it.

00:23:58.950 --> 00:24:04.960
A Surprising Client

00:24:04.960 --> 00:24:10.460
Let's ask her ourselves.
